The group performed the song as a finale when they appeared in the 1986 episode "Cowboy George" of ''[[The A-Team]]''. Likely because of the line "I'm a man without conviction" and the chorus, which includes the word ''[[chameleon]]'', "Karma Chameleon" has been used by several politicians in political adverts. In 2006, Britain's [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] used "Karma Chameleon" as the theme song for a [[Dave the Chameleon|series of political advertisements]] against [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] leader [[David Cameron]] in the [[2006 United Kingdom local elections|2006 UK local elections]].<ref>{{cite news|first= Ann |last= Treneman |title= Dave and Labour's bad karma chameleon |newspaper= [[The Sunday Times]] |date= 19 April 2006 |url= http://www.timesonline.co.uk/tol/news/politics/article1082818.ece |archive-date= 21 November 2008 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20081121071924/http://www.timesonline.co.uk/tol/news/politics/article1082818.ece}}</ref>

[[BT Group|BT]] used "Karma Chameleon" in a [[television advertisement]] in the [[United Kingdom]] in 2002 featuring a phone with a singing and talking chameleon. The advertisement got so popular that a variant of the phone was produced and marketed in both the United Kingdom and [[United States]] (the latter through an [[infomercial]] featuring Boy George's "approval"). 

The song also appears in the fictional radio station The Mix 107.77 for the game ''[[Saints Row 2]]''. The song is also performed in Virgin Cruise's "The Voyage" advertisement.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harrison |first=James |date=10 January 2023 |title=Karma Chameleon! Virgin Voyages invites 80's nostalgia in new campaign |url=https://www.travelweekly.com.au/article/karma-chameleon-virgin-voyages-invites-80s-nostalgia-in-new-campaign/ |access-date=24 January 2024 |website=Travel Weekly}}</ref><ref>{{Cite press release |date=6 January 2023 |title=Virgin Voyages Takes Future Sailors on Musically Guided Cinematic Journey at Sea |url=https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/virgin-voyages-takes-future-sailors-on-musically-guided-cinematic-journey-at-sea-301715487.html |access-date=24 January 2024 |agency=PR Newswire|quote=The video is musically guided by a reimagining of Culture Club's iconic, 1983 song, "Karma Chameleon," featuring pop-artist Drew Love.}}</ref> The song has also appeared in ''[[Romy and Michele's High School Reunion]]'', ''[[Rock Star (2001 film)|Rock Star]]'', ''[[Scary Movie 4]]'', ''[[The Call (2013 film)|The Call]]'', ''[[Sex Tape (film)|Sex Tape]]'', ''[[American Dad!]]'', ''[[Ricky Stanicky]]'', and ''[[Despicable Me 4]]''.{{citation needed|date=June 2026}}

